    "q-134236": {
      "dom_id": "question-134236",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "After Sophia takes her share of walnuts, Robert's remaining amount of walnuts is\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \nthan Susan's amount of walnuts because $2\\,\\frac{2}{5}$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         $\\frac{17}{9}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Robert has $2\\,\\frac{2}{5}$ pounds of walnuts remaining, and Susan has $\\frac{17}{9}$ pounds of walnuts.\n\nWe cannot compare the fractions directly as they don't have a common denominator.\n\nWe can make a common denominator of $5\\times 9=45.$\n\nTo put $2\\,\\frac{2}{5}$ over a denominator of $45,$ we first convert to an improper fraction and then multiply the numerator and denominator by $9:$\n\n$$\n2\\,\\frac{2}{5}=\\frac{12}{5}=\\frac{12\\times 9}{5\\times 9}=\\frac{108}{45}\n$$\n\nTo put $\\frac{17}{9}$ over a denominator of $45,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{17}{9}=\\frac{17\\times 5}{9\\times 5}=\\frac{85}{45}\n$$\n\nWe can now compare the fractions $\\frac{108}{45}$ and $\\frac{85}{45}$ by looking at the numerators only.\n\nSince $108>85,$ the correct statement must be:\n\n$$\n\\frac{108}{45}>\\frac{85}{45}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is\n\n\"After Sophia takes her walnuts, Robert's remaining amount of walnuts is $>$ than Susan's amount of walnuts because $2\\,\\frac{2}{5}>\\frac{17}{9}.$\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
